    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThere are several changes in how command-line window behaves after #40325 \n\n- Opening empty command-line window shows two empty lines instead of one: `nvim --clean` + `q:` - see two blank lines instead of one on Neovim 0.12.3.\n- The `<CR>` is a buffer-local mapping which can (and did) break plugins that rely on setting custom behavior in command-line window. I don't see a way to implement this differently if \"regular buffer\" approach is to stay, though. But at least this should be documented in the news and probably in the `:h cmdwin`.\n- The statuscolumn now adds a space after `:`. This is probably intended, but I think preserving the previous approach without extra space (which mimics how the text is shown in a regular command line) looks better.\n- The buffer is not listed, while previously it was listed. I.e. executing `:echo buflisted(nvim_get_current_buf())` with command-line window now active now shows 1 instead of 0.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean`\n2. `q:`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIdeally - full compatibility with the previous command-line window behavior. Where not possible - explicitly document this with possible workarounds.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-823+gb9b1992d9d\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.0.12-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage",
