        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> It's possible to drive it as a builtin instead of a mapping, I just judged that the mapping feels more flexible / less magical.\n\nThe problem is that with buffer-local mapping it is more awkward for users/plugins to emulate the \"execute current line\" action. Previously both `nnoremap <CR> <CR>` (to reset global `<CR>` mapping) and `feedkeys('\\r', 'n')` (to execute current line) worked as expected. If there is an exported and documented `vim.cmdwin.confirm`, then it would probably be okay, but I have a feeling that this is a bit too much.",
